        "box"
      ],
      "command": "printf '' > /data/de; ( exec <&-; cat; echo rc=$?; exec < /data/de; cat; echo rc=$? ); ( exec 0<&1; cat; echo rc=$? ); ( exec 0<&2; cat; echo rc=$? ); rm /data/de",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "rc=1\nrc=0\nrc=1\nrc=1\n",
        "stderr": "cat: -: Bad file descriptor\ncat: -: Bad file descriptor\ncat: -: Bad file descriptor\n"
      },
      "note": "bash also prints `cat: closing standard input: Bad file descriptor` after the first line, cat's close of an already-closed fd 0; mirage's cat has no descriptor to close and prints the read failure only."
    },
